description_json:
{"play_by_play": "A video clip featuring an interview with an All Blacks coach speaking about his Cook Island Māori heritage and coaching philosophy.

Coach: "Yeah look, um, I'm really proud to be Cook Island Māori. My mum grew up in Titikaveka in Rarotonga. She's an amazing woman, really inspirational and had a massive impact on the lives of us kids. So I know she'll be looking down with pride today. I think it's about people, like you know, I've been lucky enough to work with fantastic people across the globe. I've learnt a lot from that. I'm probably the type of coach who gets an arm around people while I'm jabbing them in the ribs. You know, like I care about people. I think people want to know that you care, but you know I'll also be driving them to be the best they can be."

The video concludes with text on screen reading: "WELCOME COACH."", "content_theme": ["player story"], "format_access": ["interview", "announcement", "behind-the-scenes"], "people": ["all blacks"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad"], "event": ["all blacks"], "tone": ["pride", "wholesome"], "context": ["announcement", "press conference"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Black Fern Martha Mataele delivers an emotional presentation speech for her younger sister Atlanta Lolohea's debut jersey (#16) in front of the team.

Martha Mataele: "Sorry... It's an honour to be able to present my sister's debut jersey. Atlanta... Most of our family couldn't make it from New Zealand, but they wanted me to pass on that they're so proud of you. And, so would Uncle Jeff. Sorry. Just watching your journey and just, I guess, early on in your career, coming back from a shoulder injury and then redoing your shoulder again and just watching you come back from that shows your resilience and just the person that you are. As your older sister, I'm so proud of you. This is all God's timing, and I know you've put all your faith in Him, and, oh, I just can't explain how proud I am and that I get to present this jersey to you. And you have a whole village beside you, and not all of them could make it, but they're here in spirit. And, yeah, congrats."

Atlanta Lolohea steps forward to hug her sister and accept the jersey while their teammates applaud and sing in celebration.", "content_theme": ["player story", "celebration"], "format_access": ["behind-the-scenes", "candid clip"], "people": ["martha mataele", "atlanta lolohea", "black ferns"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad"], "event": ["black ferns"], "tone": ["wholesome", "pride"], "context": ["jersey reveal"], "overall_team": ["women"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Jack Goodhue: We're here in Wellington. We've got four teams here who are in a mini competition in the build-up for the Christchurch Special Olympics. Great energy here. We've got the Wellington Wildcats, that's my team at the moment. Wildcats on 3. 1, 2, 3, Wildcats! Such a great event, looking forward to seeing these guys and more teams down in Christchurch on the 8th of December.

Asafo Aumua: Good to see the talent out here, coming from a background where I was a teacher aide in special needs, it's good to see these kids get amongst it. There's heaps of skill here, and I know that the people down in Christchurch are in for a real big show. So make sure that you guys come along.

Group: 1, 2, 3, All Blacks!", "content_theme": ["player story", "non rugby related"], "format_access": ["behind-the-scenes", "interview"], "people": ["jack goodhue", "asafo aumua", "all blacks"], "brands": ["adidas", "toyota", "special olympics"], "event": ["olympics", "all blacks"], "tone": ["wholesome", "lighthearted", "pride"], "context": ["tour", "off-season"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Paul Single, a dedicated All Blacks fan, shares his experience traveling the world for over 30 years to attend nearly 100 live matches across multiple countries alongside his wife, expressing his deep passion and pride for the All Blacks.

Transcript:
"Well, I've probably calculated over the last 30 something years, I've probably nearly hit 100 games I've been to. I think I've seen 7 different countries. I've done Scotland, France, Wales, Italy, London, obviously New Zealand, Australia. You can't beat live. Each one holds an individual warmth in my heart, and travelling with my wife, obviously she's always been with me to make sure that I behave myself. New Zealand becomes very popular as soon as you mention you're a Kiwi and then you mention the All Blacks, and always people say, well, we love the All Blacks."", "content_theme": ["player story"], "format_access": ["interview", "montage", "promotion"], "people": ["paul single", "all blacks"], "brands": ["altrad", "adidas"], "event": ["all blacks", "world cup"], "tone": ["pride", "wholesome", "nostalgia"], "context": ["tour", "travel"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Ian Foster: "They're a company that's very passionate about what they do, they... they want to win. So that's two pretty good qualities that we share. So I think there's a bit of synergy there, and I guess for us to feel that and to I guess put a smile on their face, it's pretty cool."

Bjørn Gulden: "There is no team that I know that has an impact like your team. The story about the All Blacks is very unique. No, I wasn't surprised about the number of people, but I was touched by how people reacted. I mean, being an All Black player must be... I'm going to dream tonight that I'm an All Black player!"

Faye Moyle: "I've lived in Germany for 17 years, but I've never ever lost my passion for the All Blacks, and it's like literally a dream fantasy come true... I couldn't be prouder."", "content_theme": ["haka", "non rugby related"], "format_access": ["interview", "montage", "behind-the-scenes", "promotion"], "people": ["ian foster", "sam cane", "beauden barrett", "aaron smith", "bjørn gulden", "faye moyle", "all blacks"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad", "ineos"], "event": ["all blacks", "world cup"], "tone": ["excitement", "pride", "wholesome"], "context": ["tour"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Speaker 1 (Dame Patsy Reddy): "I have the great honor to announce the 32-man squad against England and against Fiji: George Bell, Billy Proctor, Cortez Ratima, Wallace Sititi, Pasilio Tosi... Congratulations once again, and Kia Kaha, Kapa O Pango."

Speaker 2 (Scott Robertson): "A lot of work has been done getting to this point, and I'd like to acknowledge the selectors, the coaching group. I'd like to announce and congratulate Scott Barrett as All Black captain."

Speaker 3 (Scott Barrett): "Yeah, I'm hugely honored and grateful for the opportunity to, yeah, captain the All Blacks. And understand there's a lot of pressure that goes with it, but excited to see where this team's going."", "content_theme": ["player story", "celebration", "non rugby related"], "format_access": ["announcement", "interview", "montage", "reaction"], "people": ["scott barrett", "scott robertson", "cortez ratima", "pasilio tosi", "george bell", "billy proctor", "wallace sititi", "all blacks"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad", "sky", "ineos"], "event": ["all blacks"], "tone": ["pride", "excitement", "wholesome"], "context": ["squad naming", "announcement", "press conference"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "00:00 - 00:25: Arihiana Marino-Tauhinu passes to Ruahei Demant, who breaks through the defensive line before offloading to Renee Holmes. Holmes links up with Ayesha Leti-I'iga, who surges down the touchline to score a try in the corner for the Black Ferns.

00:26 - 00:44: Kendra Reynolds fends off a defender and offloads to Ayesha Leti-I'iga, who charges through the defensive line to score her second try of the match.

00:45 - 01:00: Arihiana Marino-Tauhinu completes a pop pass to Ayesha Leti-I'iga, who speeds past the final defender to score her hat-trick try as commentators celebrate her performance.", "content_theme": ["try", "run"], "format_access": ["highlight"], "people": ["ayesha leti-i'iga", "arihiana marino-tauhinu", "renee holmes", "kendra reynolds", "ruahei demant", "black ferns"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad", "ineos", "tudor", "rothbury"], "event": ["pac4"], "tone": ["excitement"], "context": ["match day"], "overall_team": ["women"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

{"play_by_play": "Commentator: Win that final, unreal. And that's some good work down the front. Here's Kalounivale! First try of the World Champs!
Commentator 2: Nice set-piece play from the Black Ferns. First try of the match, Tanya Kalounivale. A little dummy to Ponsonby the hooker, and you weren't going to stop her.

A Black Ferns player throws the ball into a lineout against Australia. The Black Ferns win the lineout and set up a play, passing to prop Tanya Kalounivale (#3). Kalounivale sells a dummy, breaks through the defense line, and powers over the try line to score. Her teammates rush in to celebrate the try. A replay follows showing Kalounivale's powerful run and touchdown.", "content_theme": ["try", "celebration", "run"], "format_access": ["highlight"], "people": ["tanya kalounivale", "black ferns", "wallaroos"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad", "gilbert", "buildcorp"], "event": ["pac4", "reilly"], "tone": ["excitement"], "context": ["match day"], "overall_team": ["women"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

{"play_by_play": "Interviewer: What's the message to all the fans back back in NZ?

Player 1: Oh, we appreciate them, hey. It's been unreal the support we've received, you know. Just so, yeah like I said, so grateful to be here and, you know, we represent our whole country, that's like five million people. So, with heavy hands, you know, we carry it, but up to the task as well, yeah.

Player 2: Just thank you all for the love and the support, thank you for tuning in each week. The boys got it done and, um, yeah, just over the moon. Yeah, just thanks a lot, NZ, and I'll see you guys soon, and Happy Mother's Day.", "content_theme": ["player story", "training"], "format_access": ["interview", "montage"], "people": ["new zealand u20 rugby team"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad", "ineos"], "event": ["u20", "trc"], "tone": ["pride", "wholesome"], "context": ["post-match"], "overall_team": ["youth", "men"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

{"play_by_play": "Steven speaks on a community sports field during a social tag rugby session: "When I got here in 2013, I was fortunate to be part of the rugby team at my high school, Rangitoto College. And I loved it, you know, the intensity, the teamwork, and all the friends you get to make with them. And especially for someone new to the country, able to really get into that local atmosphere, you know, rock up every Saturday morning. It's different, right? You know it. And through all these years, I realized that I never really see another Chinese face or Asian face in that regard, and I feel that they're really missing out. So that's why I sort of started saying that perhaps we should make a program to sort of figure out why is there such a low participation numbers and how we can get our number up, or at least give everyone a shot, right? It's fine if they don't like the sport, but if they never had a chance, then that's really gutting. The feedback was overwhelming. We got 95% five-star ratings, everyone just loved it and they want more."

A female participant shares her thoughts: "I think this is a great pathway. Otherwise it would be so daunting. Steven has also organized a few Blues games to go to watch and just like, I feel like you really embedded yourself into the rugby culture now."

A male participant adds: "Yeah, and we really appreciate, you know, all the support from different places. Otherwise, I wouldn't be able to have that sort of chance to really play rugby."", "content_theme": ["player story"], "format_access": ["interview", "montage", "candid clip"], "people": ["undefined"], "brands": ["nike"], "event": ["undefined"], "tone": ["pride", "wholesome"], "context": ["award"], "overall_team": ["men", "women", "youth"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "A member of the Black Ferns Sevens team records a selfie video on the field surrounded by her teammates holding trophies and medals after a tournament win.

Speaker: "Kia ora whānau! Just a message to everybody back home, thank you for all the support. We love it, we can feel it all the way over here in NYC. Big love!"

The players cheer loudly, waving their medals and trophies towards the camera.", "content_theme": ["celebration"], "format_access": ["candid clip"], "people": ["black ferns sevens", "new zealand rugby team"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad"], "event": ["hsbc svns", "sevens"], "tone": ["excitement", "pride"], "context": ["post-match"], "overall_team": ["women"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

{"play_by_play": "Interviewer: "What do you think she would think about what you've achieved?"

Sarah Hirini gets emotional while holding her Olympic gold medal and reflects on her early career:

Sarah Hirini: "She'd be pretty happy. That person back then got invited to a rugby day for a coach Rob Jones, and he surprised me at the Olympics. To be honest, I don't know how he did it. He texted me the day of our first game, and he was like, 'I'll see you soon Mate.' And I just wrote back, 'There's no way you're here.' When I think back to that kid at Feilding High School, I instantly think of Rob Jones as well, and to have him there in the stands... he watched with my husband and my family, and I was, yeah, pretty happy to see him after the game as well. To me that sums up the start of my journey, and to that point in my career is the people I've had right from the start will still be there, even towards the end of my career."", "content_theme": ["player story"], "format_access": ["interview", "archive", "montage"], "people": ["sarah hirini", "rob jones"], "brands": ["adidas", "aig", "kukri", "nzr+"], "event": ["olympics", "sevens"], "tone": ["pride", "nostalgia", "wholesome"], "context": ["off-season"], "overall_team": ["women"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Commentator 1: "...right over the top of this. It's been ripped away by Roigard! Oh, what a brilliant try by Cameron Roigard! He's stolen that one right in front of the French faces."
Commentator 2: "Massive. Absolutely massive from the All Blacks. First and foremost the pack, 'cause they put real heat on at scrum time..."

Cam Roigard rips the ball from the breakdown, breaks through the defense, runs down the field to score a try, and celebrates with his All Blacks teammates.", "content_theme": ["try", "run", "celebration"], "format_access": ["highlight"], "people": ["cameron roigard", "all blacks", "france rugby team"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad"], "event": ["all blacks"], "tone": ["excitement"], "context": ["match day"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

{"play_by_play": "Male All Blacks rugby player 1: "Great win, a little bit messy in the second half, but um, awesome to be able to come over and play the Brave Blossoms. They're never an easy side to to play against. Kind of a great crowd as well, so happy with that one. Great start to the to the tour."

Male All Blacks rugby player 2: "Nah, awesome to see his debut today. Unreal, too. Yeah, shoutout to the Waikato boys who won too, now. Um, nah, awesome to see his debut and all his family coming down twice. You know, it's unreal. Way for for him to start his All Black career, so nah, just proud of him, bro."

Male All Blacks rugby player 3: "I think it's probably special because, um, you know, especially for the new caps, Ruben and and Pete. Both getting on the field and doing really well, so I'm rapt for them. Opportunity to join the legacy and in a beautiful part of the world to play as well."", "content_theme": ["player story"], "format_access": ["interview", "candid clip"], "people": ["all blacks rugby team"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad"], "event": ["all blacks"], "tone": ["pride", "wholesome"], "context": ["post-match", "tour"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice", "ambient"]}

{"play_by_play": "An All Blacks player kicks the ball high downfield during a match against Australia. Jordie Barrett leaps high in the air to compete for the aerial ball against an Australian defender, successfully securing the catch before landing safely and calling for a mark. Replays highlight his focus and skill under the high ball.

Commentary:
"Jordan puts a kick up this time. Sending it high. Toole there for Australia. And excellently done. That concentration, never takes his eyes off the ball. He's got his eyes on the ball as well. Holds on and calls the mark. Excellent from Jordie Barrett. Really, really good, wasn't it."", "content_theme": ["kick", "rugby_skills"], "format_access": ["highlight"], "people": ["jordie barrett", "will jordan", "all blacks", "australia rugby team"], "brands": ["tudor", "asics", "ihg", "flight centre", "bet365", "cadbury"], "event": ["trc", "all blacks"], "tone": ["excitement"], "context": ["match day"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

{"play_by_play": "00:00 - 00:19: Commentary: 'Now Collins goes again. Collins bursting up the middle. Now looking for some support. Couldn't find it so he held on. 20 meters out. Devine now to Spencer. Spencer running hard, lobs it over the top. Rokocoko goes in! And there's the first try of the test.' New Zealand forward Jerry Collins breaks through the French line. The ball is recycled through Craig Devine and Carlos Spencer, who lobs a pass to Joe Rokocoko on the wing to score the first try.

00:20 - 00:32: Commentary: 'He's not the target, it's Chris Jack beautifully taken. As Devine feeds Spencer. Rokocoko stretching! He's got too much pace I think. Should go all the way! What a good try! Fantastic.' The All Blacks win a lineout through Chris Jack. Devine feeds Spencer, who passes wide to Joe Rokocoko. Rokocoko sprints down the left wing, outrunning the defense to score his second try.

00:33 - 00:44: Commentary: 'He gets it off to Spencer, Umaga, Muliaina, wide to Rokocoko, he's got another one! That's a hat-trick!' Quick passing across the backline from Spencer to Tana Umaga, then Mils Muliaina out to Joe Rokocoko on the wing, who dives over the try line to complete his hat-trick against France.", "content_theme": ["try", "run"], "format_access": ["highlight", "archive"], "people": ["joe rokocoko", "jerry collins", "carlos spencer", "tana umaga", "mils muliaina", "chris jack", "craig devine", "new zealand rugby team", "france rugby team"], "brands": ["philips", "steinlager", "adecco"], "event": ["all blacks"], "tone": ["excitement", "nostalgia"], "context": ["match day"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

{"play_by_play": "A speaker shares his experience with early coaches and his coaching approach while vintage photos and clips of him coaching junior rugby are shown:

"I had some really good early coaches that were always really focused on the positive side of it, and what you're good at, and telling you what they want to see, and want to see that again from me, 'Can you please do that?' I just remember the little stories or the little simple things that created a mindset for me from these coaches and just how they framed it. And I had in my head beforehand and it was normally positive. I forgot the negative stuff, or if I did, I didn't want to race for them or play for them. I coach my son's all the way through their junior grade rugby, and I just try and pass on all those things that I learned to them as well."

The video ends with the "Balance is Better" and New Zealand Rugby logos.", "content_theme": ["player story", "training"], "format_access": ["interview", "promotion"], "people": ["undefined"], "brands": ["new zealand rugby", "sport new zealand", "paknsave"], "event": ["undefined"], "tone": ["nostalgia", "wholesome", "pride"], "context": ["off-season"], "overall_team": ["youth", "men"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Maiakawanakaulani Roos introduces herself as a Balance is Better Champion. She shares her story about participating in various sports during her youth, supported by her parents, and how developing skills across multiple sports helped her transition into playing rugby for the Black Ferns. Footage includes her match appearances with the Black Ferns alongside photo montages of her participating in canoeing, softball, volleyball, netball, and youth rugby.

Transcript:
"Hi, I'm Maiakawanakaulani and I'm your Balance is Better champion. I was really lucky when I was young because my parents supported me in anything I wanted to do. So I played a bunch of sports. I played basketball, did some gymnastics. At our school we had like people come in and they introduced us to other sports like Taekwondo, AFL, soccer, football, all of those kind of things. I was really keen to give everything a go, and that's kind of carried through to high school and to now. I think the benefits of playing multiple sports in school is you get a wide range of skills and they all transfer into different sports. My skills from netball, like agility and that, transferred into rugby."", "content_theme": ["player story"], "format_access": ["interview", "promotion", "montage"], "people": ["maiakawanakaulani roos", "black ferns", "netball", "basketball", "volleyball", "softball", "afl", "taekwondo", "soccer"], "brands": ["sky sport", "adidas", "new zealand rugby", "balance is better"], "event": ["world cup", "black ferns"], "tone": ["wholesome", "pride", "lighthearted"], "context": ["gym", "off-season"], "overall_team": ["women", "youth"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Three young Black Ferns players speak to the camera at the All Blacks Experience event announcing the inaugural Women's Lions Tour in 2027:

'We're just here at All Blacks Experience at the announcement of the first women's Lions Tour happening in 2027, so... Yes, we've had the honor of us three being here, the youngest in the Black Ferns team. We've met a lot of very cool people and it's cool to see the efforts that have gone into making this competition happen because obviously it's very huge, so... yeah, I think we're just very grateful to be here, very excited to think forward at 2027. We will be 23, 24, 25, and so we're kind of still babies by then, so hopefully we're at our peak by the time it comes around, so very exciting.'

Intercut clips show the players posing for photos with officials, chatting with attendees, and taking part in media interviews, concluding with the Black Ferns and British & Irish Lions logos.", "content_theme": ["player story"], "format_access": ["announcement", "interview", "promotion"], "people": ["black ferns"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad", "ineos", "rnz"], "event": ["lions tour"], "tone": ["excitement", "pride", "lighthearted"], "context": ["announcement", "tour"], "overall_team": ["women"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "Jordi Viljoen: "Hey, I'm Jordi Viljoen from the New Zealand Under 20 squad. The lads and I just wanted to let you know that we are playing two test matches against Australia Under 20s. We're playing first test on the 29th of May at NZCIS in Upper Hutt, and we're playing our second test on the 3rd of June at Sky Stadium."

Male Player 2: "The second match is also a double header to the Hurricanes vs Crusaders DHL Super Rugby Pacific match, which kicks off at 4:30 at Sky Stadium. So lock it in your diaries and bring the family along for a great day of footy."

Male Player 3: "The two matches against Australia start our build-up for the Under 20s World Cup in June and July, so there's plenty to play for in 2023."", "content_theme": ["rivalry"], "format_access": ["announcement", "promotion"], "people": ["jordi viljoen", "new zealand under 20", "australia under 20", "hurricanes", "crusaders"], "brands": ["adidas", "ineos", "altrad", "sky", "dhl"], "event": ["u20", "super rugby pacific", "world cup"], "tone": ["excitement", "pride"], "context": ["announcement", "pre-match"], "overall_team": ["youth", "men"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

{"play_by_play": "Will Jordan speaks while clips of him playing interactive games, playing golf, and training in the gym are shown.

Will Jordan: "Fundamentally, I think it's about being healthy, and I think being active is huge for both your mental and physical health. Going back to the golf, like at the moment, when I'm playing rugby, if things aren't going well, it's a huge release for me to be able to go out there and just take my mind off it and have some fun. I guess the more official side of it with rugby, we're more focused on the process around what we're doing, how we're getting better each day, rather than necessarily looking at results. You have your setbacks and you have your tough times, but knowing that there's always a brighter future ahead has been huge, and remembering that everything's temporary. Things don't always go your way, but having the resilience to bounce back and keep giving things a go is, I think, a really important characteristic in sport, and yeah, going out there and just trying to improve day-to-day is huge."

The video ends with the team in a huddle shouting in unison, followed by text on screen reading: 'THE HOME OF YOUTH SPORT IN NEW ZEALAND - BALANCE IS BETTER'.", "content_theme": ["player story", "training", "non rugby related"], "format_access": ["interview", "montage", "promotion"], "people": ["will jordan", "all blacks"], "brands": ["adidas", "altrad", "ineos"], "event": ["all blacks"], "tone": ["wholesome", "pride"], "context": ["gym", "off-season"], "overall_team": ["men"], "audio_format": ["voice", "song"]}

{"play_by_play": "The Black Ferns execute a rapid attack from a breakdown against the USA women's rugby team. The ball is passed out to Ayesha Leti-I'iga, who fends off multiple USA defenders, powers through the line, and dives over to score a impressive try. Replay angles highlight her powerful running and tackling resistance.

Commentator 1: "Mikaele-Tu'u... Now Kendra Reynolds... fends the first off... Leti-I'iga! Leti-I'iga goes through again! What can't she do? What can't she do?"

Commentator 2: "That rugby is just so hard to defend. USA don't know whether they've got to cover the offload or make the tackle, and... definitely paying off for the Black Ferns."", "content_theme": ["try", "run", "tackle", "rugby_skills"], "format_access": ["highlight"], "people": ["black ferns", "usa rugby team", "ayesha leti-i'iga", "kendra reynolds", "liana mikaele-tu'u"], "brands": ["ineos", "castore"], "event": ["pac4"], "tone": ["excitement"], "context": ["match day"], "overall_team": ["women"], "audio_format": ["voice"]}

